    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386-a3">

                <pb facs="0539" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg437"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Furniss to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 270.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have recently received instructions from
                    my Government as follows:</p>
                <p>“Now, that the American legation and consulates have been cleared of refugees,
                    you will make it distinctly known that no more Haitian refugees will be admitted
                    to shelter by you or your subordinates.”</p>
                <p>This is communicated to your excellency with the request that you will assist
                    this legation in giving publicity thereto.</p>
                <p>Your excellency will please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
